WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:09.275
Hi! I'm Snowshoe Rabbit. I'm looking for something to eat.

2
00:00:09.276 --> 00:00:14.433
But it is not very easy because the forest is covered with snow and the trees are bare.

3
00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:20.464
During the winter people have nice warm houses to live in, but animals have to stay outside.

4
00:00:20.465 --> 00:00:24.643
So we have to do different things to survive the cold.

5
00:00:24.644 --> 00:00:30.183
During the winter, you don't see many birds in the forest because most of them have migrated.

6
00:00:30.184 --> 00:00:36.356
In the fall, when the weather gets cool, the birds gather together and fly south to warmer places.

7
00:00:36.357 --> 00:00:41.660
When people travel, they use maps, but birds travel without using any maps.

8
00:00:41.661 --> 00:00:47.161
It is amazing that they never get lost; they know exactly where to go.

9
00:00:47.162 --> 00:00:51.175
Some birds use the sun, the moon, and the stars to guide them.

10
00:00:51.176 --> 00:00:54.109
Birds are not the only creatures that migrate.

11
00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:59.381
The monarch butterfly flies all the way from the Rocky Mountains in Canada to Mexico.

12
00:00:59.382 --> 00:01:08.526
Some deer that live in the Arctic, like the caribou, travel hundreds of miles to find grasses and plants to eat during the winter months.

13
00:01:08.527 --> 00:01:12.377
Even some ladybugs and snakes travel before the winter.

14
00:01:12.378 --> 00:01:15.839
But many animals stay in the forest all winter long.

15
00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:20.535
Sometimes you can see deer, foxes, and rabbits like me in the wintertime.

16
00:01:20.536 --> 00:01:23.665
We don't go away because we like the winter.

17
00:01:23.666 --> 00:01:30.736
In the winter, we eat whatever we can find, like moss, twigs, bark, and leaves.

18
00:01:30.737 --> 00:01:35.294
In order to get ready for winter, we grow new, thicker fur in the fall.

19
00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:38.395
My new fur is white to help me hide in the snow.

20
00:01:38.396 --> 00:01:45.608
Squirrels, mice, and beavers get ready for winter by gathering extra food and storing it in a safe place to eat later.

21
00:01:45.609 --> 00:01:52.520
Many animals sleep during winter, like bats, squirrels, skunks, chipmunks, and bears.

22
00:01:52.521 --> 00:01:55.574
Sleeping during the winter is called hibernation.

23
00:01:55.575 --> 00:02:01.023
By hibernating, these animals save energy and are able to live on very little food.

24
00:02:01.024 --> 00:02:04.731
Before winter they find a safe, warm place to sleep.

25
00:02:04.732 --> 00:02:10.103
Some have dens under the ground; others sleep on the ground underneath the fallen leaves.

26
00:02:10.104 --> 00:02:16.199
If lots of snow falls, it can actually help them stay warm, like a thick blanket.

27
00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:21.904
Some mice sleep in dens together with many others so that they all help each other to stay warm.

28
00:02:21.905 --> 00:02:26.174
Chipmunks, squirrels, and some other animals are called true hibernators.

29
00:02:26.175 --> 00:02:33.742
When true hibernators sleep, the temperature of their body decreases and their heart slows down, so they need less food.

30
00:02:33.743 --> 00:02:38.832
In fact, when you see true hibernating animals, they look like they are dead.

31
00:02:38.833 --> 00:02:41.667
If you touch them, they feel very cold.

32
00:02:41.668 --> 00:02:45.860
Other animals, like bears, sleep most of the winter as well.

33
00:02:45.861 --> 00:02:51.257
They are not true hibernators, however, because their body temperature cannot decrease.

34
00:02:51.258 --> 00:02:56.725
In order to stay warm while they hibernate, bears need to eat huge amounts of food in the fall.

35
00:02:56.726 --> 00:03:01.276
The extra fat stores energy to keep them warm while they sleep.

36
00:03:01.277 --> 00:03:05.532
By the time spring comes, the bears have lost most of their fat.

37
00:03:05.533 --> 00:03:08.782
Actually, animals do not sleep all winter long.

38
00:03:08.783 --> 00:03:14.532
Some animals can sleep for one month, but many animals only sleep for a few days at a time.

39
00:03:14.533 --> 00:03:21.410
When they get hungry, they wake up for a little while and eat some of their food.

40
00:03:21.411 --> 00:03:26.968
Many hibernating animals have a place in their little homes where they can go to the toilet.

41
00:03:26.969 --> 00:03:30.410
Also if the animals get too cold, they might die.

42
00:03:30.411 --> 00:03:35.734
So on very cold days, many animals wake up and get warm by shivering.

43
00:03:35.735 --> 00:03:39.047
In the pond many animals hibernate as well.

44
00:03:39.048 --> 00:03:44.603
Some turtles and frogs swim to the bottom of the pond before the water freezes.

45
00:03:44.604 --> 00:03:50.200
They dig a little hole in the mud at the bottom and spend the winter sleeping beneath the frozen ice.

46
00:03:50.201 --> 00:03:51.854
What about the fish?

47
00:03:51.855 --> 00:03:55.783
Have you ever wondered what happens to the fish when the water is frozen?

48
00:03:55.784 --> 00:04:00.574
Most fish stay awake for the winter, but they are very quiet and still.

49
00:04:00.575 --> 00:04:07.582
They go down to the bottom of the pond where the water is not frozen and wait for spring to come.

50
00:04:07.583 --> 00:04:09.716
It's lonely here in the winter.

51
00:04:09.717 --> 00:04:16.087
But after their long sleep, my animal friends will come out of their houses and enjoy a fresh new spring.

52
00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:17.188
Chirp, chirp!

53
00:04:17.189 --> 00:04:23.565
I think I hear the birds coming! Wake up everyone! It's spring!
